BANKWISE DEMO BANK
CREDIT CARD SERVICES GUIDE

1. INTRODUCTION

A credit card is a payment instrument that allows an eligible customer to make purchases using a credit facility provided by the card issuer. The customer is required to repay the amount according to the applicable billing terms.

This is a fictional/demo document created for the BankWise AI RAG project. It is not an official banking policy.

2. CREDIT CARD FEATURES

Common credit card features may include:

• Purchases at participating merchants
• Online payments
• Contactless payments where supported
• Recurring payment support where available
• Transaction statements
• Reward or cashback programs on eligible cards
• EMI or installment options where offered

Features depend on the specific card and bank.

3. CREDIT LIMIT

A credit limit is the maximum amount that a cardholder can generally use at a given time under the card's terms.

The credit limit may depend on factors such as:
• Customer eligibility
• Income information
• Credit history
• Existing obligations
• Bank policies
• Card type

The bank may periodically review the credit limit.

4. BILLING CYCLE

A billing cycle is a period during which eligible credit card transactions are recorded.

At the end of the billing cycle, the card issuer generally provides a statement containing information such as:
• Total amount due
• Minimum amount due
• Payment due date
• Transactions
• Applicable fees or charges

5. PAYMENT DUE DATE

The payment due date is the date by which the customer should make the required payment according to the statement.

Customers should review their statement and make payments through official banking channels before the due date.

6. MINIMUM AMOUNT DUE

A credit card statement may contain a minimum amount that must be paid by the due date.

Paying only the minimum amount may result in interest or other charges depending on the card's terms.

Customers should understand the applicable terms before choosing how much to repay.

7. CREDIT CARD FEES

Credit cards may have different types of fees or charges, including:

• Annual fees
• Late payment charges
• Cash withdrawal charges
• Foreign transaction charges
• Interest charges
• Replacement charges
• Other applicable service fees

The actual charges depend on the card and bank.

8. CREDIT CARD INTEREST

Interest may apply when the outstanding balance is not paid according to the applicable terms.

Customers should carefully read the card's interest rate, repayment terms, and applicable charges.

9. CREDIT CARD CASH WITHDRAWAL

Some credit cards may allow cash withdrawals from supported ATMs.

Cash withdrawals may have separate fees and interest rules.

Customers should check the applicable card terms before using this feature.

10. CREDIT CARD EMI

Some banks may provide EMI or installment options for eligible purchases.

The applicable:
• Interest rate
• Processing fee
• Tenure
• Eligibility
• Terms

can vary by bank and card.

11. LOST OR STOLEN CREDIT CARD

If a credit card is lost or stolen, the customer should immediately report it through an official bank channel.

Possible channels include:
• Official mobile banking application
• Internet banking
• Official customer support
• Bank branch

The customer should follow the bank's card-blocking and replacement procedure.

12. UNAUTHORIZED CREDIT CARD TRANSACTION

If a customer notices a transaction that they do not recognize, they should contact the card issuer immediately through an official channel.

Customers should keep relevant transaction details available when reporting the issue.

Never share:
• OTP
• PIN
• CVV
• Password
• Authentication codes

with unknown persons.

13. CREDIT CARD SECURITY

Customers should:
• Keep the card secure.
• Monitor statements regularly.
• Use trusted websites for online payments.
• Avoid suspicious links.
• Keep authentication information private.
• Report suspicious transactions immediately.

14. CREDIT SCORE

Credit activity may contribute to a customer's credit history and credit score according to applicable credit reporting practices.

Responsible repayment and managing credit within one's financial capacity can help maintain healthy credit behavior.

15. CREDIT CARD APPLICATION

Credit card eligibility and approval depend on the bank's policies.

An application may require information such as:
• Identity information
• Address information
• Income information
• Employment or business information
• Other documents requested by the bank

Submitting an application does not guarantee approval.

16. CREDIT CARD CLOSURE

Customers who want to close a credit card should follow the bank's official closure procedure.

Any outstanding balance or applicable dues should be settled according to the card terms before closure.

17. BANKWISE AI LIMITATION

BankWise AI is an informational chatbot created for a demonstration RAG project.

It cannot:
• Approve credit cards
• Check real credit limits
• View customer statements
• Make credit card payments
• Access customer accounts
• Retrieve card numbers
• Modify card settings

For real credit card issues, customers should contact their actual bank or card issuer through an official channel.

DISCLAIMER

Credit card eligibility, limits, interest rates, fees, rewards, repayment rules, and other conditions vary between banks and card products and may change over time. Always verify current information through the relevant bank's official channels.
